"""Wraith V2: every part traced on sheet 90 (sheet pixel coordinates). Writes parts.json.
front/rear: the part's outline in the front (or rear) view; side: in the side view (the mech's left, facing left).
kind: c = centre part (made symmetric), m = one of a mirrored pair, one = a single off-centre part (the antenna).
The outline is cut by the sheet's figure outline, so edges against the background can be traced loosely.
n: cross-section roundness (2 round, 4 rounded box, 8 nearly square)."""
import json, math, sys
def circ(cx, cy, r, k=16): return [[round(cx + r * math.cos(2 * math.pi * i / k), 1), round(cy + r * math.sin(2 * math.pi * i / k), 1)] for i in range(k)]
